    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NbtoxptncnUmZRtU5iK66L)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` at `28748be` (after #492).\n- Touches `sp-batch-report`, a new `sp-batch-report-view`, and the fix commands of `sp-bibprocess` (docs in `sp-academic.org`).\n- Conflicts with #496 are possible in `sp-bibprocess.el` / `sp-academic.org`: both edit `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors` (#496 adds a step to the chain; this PR wraps the chain in a report).\n  - Merge #496 first, then re-wrap its new step inside `sp-bibtex-lint--fix-report`'s apply function; or this one first and #496 resolves the same hunk.\n- #491 (abstract mover) and #476 (echo-help) do not touch these functions; no conflict seen.\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-4a39fy`: the cloud proxy cannot rename a branch, so it needs the number prefix from Sia (same as #496).\n- Not found: another open PR for the slow drop in the Org table report. This PR makes drop local in the new view; the Org view keeps its old (slow) behaviour.\n\n## What changed (stage 1)\n\n- New `sp-batch-report-view` (literate doc `docs/tangles/funct/sp-batch-report-view.org`): the default view, a `special-mode` buffer in the style of `vulpea-ui-schema-dashboard`.\n  - Folding sections (`TAB`, `S-TAB`) with the count at the window edge (a `display` `:align-to`, so it stays aligned on resize).\n  - One row per entry; file and Org links become labels; table sections have aligned columns; header line shows sections, entries, dropped.\n  - Items can carry an `:action` (RET runs it).\n  - No new package: `vui.el` re-renders a tree on every change, which is what made drop slow.\n- `d` / `u` only restyle the rows with that key (text properties and one fixed-width count); the report is not made again, the buffer size does not change, `g` and `A` still get the dropped keys.\n- `sp-batch-report-display` (`special` default, `org`): the Org buffer stays as `sp-batch-report-org-mode`.\n  - Reports still built as Org text (BibTeX lint report, litnote titles/refs/meta, notes filing, property preview) open in it, with the keys of their own mode merged in.\n  - `sp-batch-report-buffer-p` says whether a buffer is a report in either view.\n- Every `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-*` command (`order`, `indent`, `prefixes`, `authors`, `files`, `crossref`, `keys`) now opens the shared report first: drop (`d`), restore (`u`), refresh (`g`), apply (`A`) and stop (`k`) work in all of them.\n  - Dropped entries are kept per fix (`FILE::KEY#order`, …); the author fixes keep their old shared key, so existing dropped lists still work.\n  - `A` runs the previous flow (confirmation or batches, backup, one write) on what is left.\n- Keys unchanged (`RET`, `n`/`p`, `d`, `u`, `A`, `g`, `b`, `D`, `k`, `q`, echo-area hints), plus `TAB`/`S-TAB`; `n`/`p` now move between entries.\n\n## Stages not done yet (next PRs)\n\n- Convert the reports still built as Org text to sections of items: the BibTeX lint report (with fix buttons as `:action` items), litnote titles, references, meta fill-all, notes filing, property preview.\n- Replace the batch prompt (`a/g/s/q`) of the fix commands by progress in the report.\n- `d` on a section header to drop a whole group.\n- Fix the same slow drop in the Org view only if it is kept.\n\n## Measured (batch Emacs 29.3, cloud container, no Org loaded)\n\n- 4000 rows in 400 sections: drawn in 0.08 to 0.1 s.\n- 4800 rows in 300 sections with links and children: 0.15 s.\n- 200 drops: 4 ms in total.\n- Not measured: the Org view for comparison (Org cannot load in the container), the real vault, the GUI.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `tests/sp-batch-report-view-test.el` (12, one skipped without Org) and 3 new tests in `sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el`; the fix tests now press `A` in the report.\n- The Org-text tests of Zotero and `table-section` run with `sp-batch-report-display` `org`.\n- Compared with a baseline on `main` in the same container: no new failures. About 13 tests of `sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el` and others still fail here as on `main`, because Org cannot load in the container (missing packages); they need a run on the Mac.\n- `tools/check-tangle.sh` logic checked by tangling: the touched `.el` files match their docs (the existing drift of `sp-litnotes-meta.el` is not mine).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex` on the real vault: opens the dashboard, `TAB` folds a section, `S-TAB` folds all, count at the right edge\n- [x] `d` on a few rows: row struck through at once, section count `N of M`, header line \"dropped\" grows, no pause; `u` restores\n- [x] `g` keeps the folded sections and the dropped rows\n- [x] `RET` on a file label visits it; `o`, `c`, `C` of the author works report still work\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors` (and `-order`, `-indent`, `-prefixes`, `-files`, `-crossref`, `-keys`): the report lists candidates, nothing is written; `d` one, `g`, then `A` leaves the dropped one alone\n- [ ] `k` stops a running lint job from the report\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` and the litnote reports still open (in the Org view) with their keys\n- [ ] `(setq sp-batch-report-display 'org)` brings the Org view back for the model-based reports\n- [ ] Large report (hundreds of sections): drawing time and a run of `d d d` feel instant; paste the numbers here\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9bi8g2P4sdH8GttsS)_",
